BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open Streets on King
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260927T160000
DTSTAMP:20260909T100459Z
UID:39d47306-d5e6-5fb6-8fbd-3c32d5e07f72
DESCRIPTION:We can't wait for the last Open Streets of 2026! We had a blas
 t at this same event this past June and are looking forward to running it 
 back ⏪!\n\nOn September 27th from 10am-4pm\, you can enjoy a King Street
  East (from John St to Gage Ave) completely closed to car traffic. This op
 portunity doesn't come around very often\, so we hope to see you out ridin
 g\, rolling or strolling down the street to explore and connect with some 
 of the amazing organizations and groups and people here in Hamilton.\n\nWh
 ile you're out\, be sure to stop by our King at Barnesdale Hub to try out 
 some of our adaptive bikes\, learn more about Bike Share and our Everyone 
 Rides Initiative\, pick up or check out some of our handy resources and (o
 f course) spin our infamous prize wheel!\n\nSee you on Sunday\, September 
 27th!\nURL: https://www.everyonerides.org/open_streets
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/open_streets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Alley Cat Group Ride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260917T200000
DTSTAMP:20260909T100500Z
UID:3ef9d626-425d-5a73-8f13-b79e48818e57
DESCRIPTION:Our Annual Alley Ride is a classic! Come explore some of the i
 nfamous alleyways we have here in Hamilton on this group slow roll.\n\n
 🗓️Thursday\, September 17th\n\n⏰6:00 PM\n\n📍TBD\n\nLooking to jo
 in the ride\, but don’t have access to a bike? We’ve got you covered. 
 Register for a Pay As You Go membership and receive a promo code at the ev
 ent to cover the cost of the ride.\nURL: https://www.everyonerides.org/all
 ey_cat_group_ride
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/alley_cat_group_ride
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Books and Bikes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T133000
DTSTAMP:20260909T100459Z
UID:44d6230c-0a63-5f53-a74f-ce4b5266f059
DESCRIPTION:We're teaming up with the Office of Community Engagement to le
 ad a ride from McMaster to the Hamilton Public Library - Westdale Branch\,
  on Thursday\, September 10th at 12:30PM.\n\nDid you know you that as a st
 udent at McMaster\, you are eligible for a Hamilton Public Library card? T
 he Hamilton Public Library is an incredible resource and offers numerous F
 REE services you can take advantage of using your library card\, including
  computer access\, printing\, access to countless books\, music\, movies a
 nd more.\n\nCome out for this back to school ride using your Hamilton Bike
  Share U-Pass (already included and paid for in undergraduate and graduate
  full-time tuition fees) to learn how to access the nearest HPL to McMaste
 r - the Westdale Branch!\n\n🗓️ Thursday\, September 10th\n⏰ 12:30PM
 \n📍Forsyth at Sterling Bike Share Hub (Rainbow Crosswalk)\n🏁 HPL - W
 estdale Branch\n🚲 ~1.5km\n\nLet us know you're coming to the ride by re
 gistering for FREE using this link: https://www.tickettailor.com/events/mc
 masteroce/2338158\nURL: https://www.everyonerides.org/books_and_bikes
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/books_and_bikes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mural Ride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T120000
DTSTAMP:20260909T100459Z
UID:90e2091d-efe1-5bcd-ad66-92db91dbb3f9
DESCRIPTION:Our Annual Mural Ride is SO back and this time with a sweet su
 rprise from one of our sponsors\, Cogeco! ☀️🍦🚲\n\nJoin us on Sat
 urday\, August 8th at 10am for a slow roll from Corktown Park down to our 
 Discovery Drive Hub at Pier 8. Along our ride we'll guide you through a cu
 rated route to check out some of the outstanding street and mural art we a
 re so lucky to have here in #HamOnt. We will take time along the route to 
 snap photos and share some knowledge and insights behind some of the artis
 ts and artwork featured along our way.\n\nWe are looking forward to a swee
 t end to the ride down at our Discovery Drive Hub where we will join up wi
 th our sponsors Cogeco who will be hosting a special pop-up activation. Th
 ey'll be handing out exclusive HBS t-shirts\, vouchers for free ice cream 
 at Waterfront Scoops\, and other fun goodies! Celebrate that post ride fee
 ling in the best way possible with fun merch\, sweet treats\, the waterfro
 nt and games 🌊⛱️ you don't want to miss this!\nURL: https://www.eve
 ryonerides.org/mural_ride_2026
LOCATION:Cork Town Bike Share Hub\, Ferguson Avenue and Young St\, Hamilto
 n\, ON\, ON L8N 2M8\, Canada
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/mural_ride_2026
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eco-Ride Series with Environment Hamilton
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T203000
DTSTAMP:20260909T100500Z
UID:a38e4242-6899-57f1-8bb1-6afbdaffe7e3
DESCRIPTION:When you ride a bike\, do you notice your environment more? Ar
 e you curious about the ecological story of Hamilton? We're launching a sp
 ecial Group Ride series in partnership with Environment Hamilton this summ
 er. Each ride will focus on a particular layer of environmentalism in the 
 context of our city\, with routes and teaching oriented toward a specific 
 theme. It's a great way to learn more about Hamilton's unique ecological h
 istory and challenges\, all from the seat of a bicycle.\n\nJoin us for the
  following two rides:\n\n🌳🏙️\n\nPark to Park\n\nOn Tuesday July 28
  Environment Hamilton and Hamilton Bike Share are hosting a Park to Park B
 ike Tour leaving from the Beasley Park Bike Share Hub. The ride will be ju
 st over 10 km with stops at four different parks and will end by 8pm. In a
 ddition to Beasley Park\, riders will stop at Dundurn Castle\, Churchill P
 ark\, Victoria Park\, and will discuss green space access as it relates to
  demographics in different areas of the city.\n\n📆Tuesday\, July 28\n\n
 ⏰6:30PM-8:00PM\n\n📍Beasley Park Bike Share Hub (Elgin St at Cannon St
  E)\n\nIndustrial Impacts\, Past & Present\n\nOn Thursday August 20\, Envi
 ronment Hamilton and Hamilton Bike Share are hosting an Industrial Impacts
  Past & Present Cycling Tour leaving from the Bay at Strachan Bike Share H
 ub at the top of Bayfront Park. The ride will be just over 10 km with stop
 s and will end by 8pm. Cycling tour leads will discuss the impacts of indu
 stry\, legacy pollution\, and waste dumping.\n\n📆Thursday\, August 20\n
 \n⏰6:30pm - 8:00pm\n\n📍Bay at Strachan Bike Share Hub (Bay St N at St
 rachan St W under the Waterfront Trail sail post)\nURL: https://www.everyo
 nerides.org/eco_ride_series
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/eco_ride_series
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valley Park Seasonal Hub Launch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260715T193000
DTSTAMP:20260909T100500Z
UID:ab36ac79-08aa-56e2-b2cd-005b08c5c01f
DESCRIPTION:🚨PSA for tonight's event!🚨\nDue to smoke/air quality thi
 s afternoon\, our Valley Park Launch Event is moving inside the rec centre
 . Join us inside to beat the heat and chat about our new pilot expansion w
 ith some delicious goodies. Here's hoping the air clears and we can enjoy 
 a ride soon!\n\n---\n\nWe're excited to share our new seasonal pilot progr
 am for Summer 2026: Bike Share at Valley Park!\n\nFor the months of July a
 nd August\, you can find a Bike Share Hub in the rec centre parking lot at
  Valley Park and enjoy a bike ride on the many beautiful trails there.\n\n
 Join us for our launch event and enjoy some delicious baked goods while mi
 ngling with your neighbours from the City of Hamilton and Ward 9!\n\nWe'd 
 like to extend our thanks to Councillor Brad Clark and the leadership of W
 ard 9 for partnering with us on this exciting project. See you at the park
 !\n\n📆 Wednesday\, July 15th\n\n⏰6:30PM-7:30PM\n\n📍Hamilton Bike S
 hare Hub @ Valley Park parking lot\nURL: https://www.everyonerides.org/val
 ley_park
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/valley_park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MacMoves Waterfront Ride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T133000
DTSTAMP:20260909T100459Z
UID:b7a05d63-7f46-5a40-b99d-8362eac18b75
DESCRIPTION:Are you a McMaster student looking to explore Hamilton by bike
 ?! Come join us for a group ride departing from campus along the beautiful
  cycle-friendly Waterfront Trail! This ride is hosted in partnership with 
 the Office of Community Engagement and we could not be more excited!\n\n
 🗓️ Wednesday\, September 23rd\n\n⏰ 12:00 PM\n\n📍Meet at Forsyth 
 at Sterling Bike Share Hub\nURL: https://www.everyonerides.org/macmoves_wa
 terfront_ride
LOCATION:See post
URL:https://www.everyonerides.org/macmoves_waterfront_ride
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
